# The Warg (3/2, trample) is blocked by Cathar Commando (3/1): it assigns 1 lethal damage to the Commando and
# tramples 2 over, and the Commando's 3 damage kills it as it connects. The trigger is still put on the stack, but its
# first mode has no Wolf left to target, so only the Treasure mode is eligible and is taken without a question (the
# bare refusal; the other scenarios, where both modes are eligible, ask).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Bejeweled Warg
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Cathar Commando
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bejeweled Warg.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Cathar Commando.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Bejeweled Warg)
Bot2.Block(Cathar Commando > Bejeweled Warg)
! Bot1.Modes
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Cathar Commando
Bot1.Graveyard = Bejeweled Warg
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Treasure Token
